{"info":{"author":null,"author_email":"Hariidaran Tamilmaran <hariidaran@proton.me>","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Operating System :: Microsoft :: Windows :: Windows 11","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Topic :: Scientific/Engineering"],"description":"# aspen-pysys\n\nPython interface for Aspen HYSYS\n\n## Requirements\n\n- [Python 3.12.3](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-31213/)\n- [pywin32 Build 311](https://pypi.org/project/pywin32/311/)\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall via `pip install aspen-pysys` ([PyPI link](https://pypi.org/project/aspen-pysys/)).\n\n## User guide\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Before you can use HYSYS, ensure that the simulation case you wish to work on is already open.\n2. Once your simulation file is open, enter the following lines of code to set the package up.\n3. An indicator that you have successfully connected with your simulation file is the printing of 'Aspen HYSYS' in the shell (or in a notebook cell if you are using a Jupyter cell or something similar).\n\n```python\nfrom aspen_pysys import *\n\nHysys.init()\n```\n\nTo open a Aspen HYSYS simulation file (.hsc), use the `Hysys.open(sim_filepath)`, where `sim_filepath` is the filepath to your simulation file.\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os\n\ncurrent_filepath = Path(os.getcwd())\nsim_filepath = current_filepath / \"test_sim.hsc\"\n\nsimcase = Hysys.open(sim_filepath)\nsimcase\n```\n\n4. You can now use the aspen-pysys package in your code! Please refer to the [tutorial folder](./tutorial/) for an interactive example.","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":null,"license":null,"license_expression":"GPL-3.0-or-later","license_files":["LICENSE"],"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"aspen_pysys","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aspen_pysys/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aspen_pysys/","project_urls":{"Homepage":"https://codeberg.org/CacklingTanuki/aspen-pysys","Issues":"https://codeberg.org/CacklingTanuki/aspen-pysys/issues"},"provides_extra":null,"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aspen_pysys/0.1.0a0/","requires_dist":["pywin32>=311"],"requires_python":">=3.12.12","summary":"Python API for Aspen HYSYS","version":"0.1.0a0","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":37240264,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"CacklingTanuki"}]},"releases":{"0.1.0a0":[{"comment_text":null,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"f982224a896d9c1b804269e5c205882483cc334c900cfb3a3f72a1848675fdac","md5":"39ba9a901027d878fc83d57f22df77b8","sha256":"f1df2b0c6852c58ffc9a976835bed72061b90be20ca6bf335387b5529c374d5a"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"aspen_pysys-0.1.0a0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"39ba9a901027d878fc83d57f22df77b8","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":">=3.12.12","size":59635,"upload_time":"2026-05-20T14:30:48","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-05-20T14:30:48.012112Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/f9/82/224a896d9c1b804269e5c205882483cc334c900cfb3a3f72a1848675fdac/aspen_pysys-0.1.0a0-py3-none-any.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"a67694c31261456d8db557c2f9437f26f9ec029c29169badf5876de35df452ae","md5":"637a67d555d294cec76457f5257d73e1","sha256":"8cb0e699ee34c273a549bbaea6f39b14167692445965467d82d57b5ee318956a"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"aspen_pysys-0.1.0a0.tar.gz","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"637a67d555d294cec76457f5257d73e1","packagetype":"sdist","python_version":"source","requires_python":">=3.12.12","size":52904,"upload_time":"2026-05-20T14:30:49","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-05-20T14:30:49.332236Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/a6/76/94c31261456d8db557c2f9437f26f9ec029c29169badf5876de35df452ae/aspen_pysys-0.1.0a0.tar.gz","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null}]},"urls":[{"comment_text"